From fdebd84b9f50ec716c0fa6375e7fd07f7d9e1ac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 06:23:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: Increment unlootedCount for AoE-merged loot items
 (I-137)

Items merged from nearby corpses into the main creature's loot were not
incrementing unlootedCount, causing uint8 underflow when looted. This
made isLooted() permanently false, preventing AllLootRemovedFromCorpse()
from firing and the skinnable flag from being set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/aoe_loot.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/aoe_loot.cpp b/src/aoe_loot.cpp
index b72b515..d99111f 100644
--- a/src/aoe_loot.cpp
+++ b/src/aoe_loot.cpp
@@ -228,7 +228,11 @@ bool AOELootServer::CanPacketReceive(WorldSession* session, WorldPacket const& p
     for (const auto& item : itemsToAdd)
     {
         if (mainLoot->items.size() < MAX_LOOT_ITEMS)
+        {
             mainLoot->items.push_back(item);
+            if (!item.is_looted)
+                ++mainLoot->unlootedCount;
+        }
     }
 
     // Add quest items directly to player inventory
-- 
2.34.1


From c4211db9e84f5d4499fc340c8e30ce2ad33d3f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 06:24:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: Add SET NAMES to fix MySQL 8.4 collation mismatch
 (I-143)

MySQL 8.4 defaults connection collation to utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci, which
clashes with the module_string table's utf8mb4_unicode_ci, causing
DELETE/INSERT to fail with Error 1267 and blocking 'zep world sql
changed' until -k was passed to skip errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 data/sql/db-world/base/aoe_loot_module_string.sql | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/data/sql/db-world/base/aoe_loot_module_string.sql b/data/sql/db-world/base/aoe_loot_module_string.sql
index eb99b3a..f237d5f 100644
--- a/data/sql/db-world/base/aoe_loot_module_string.sql
+++ b/data/sql/db-world/base/aoe_loot_module_string.sql
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+SET NAMES utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
 SET @MODULE_STRING := 'mod-aoe-loot';
 
 -- module string
-- 
2.34.1

